= La zona

It happened without a ceremony, the way real things do: a stretch of the sierra where the army now comes only in strength and leaves as fast as it can, where the schoolteacher answers to an assembly and not a supervisor, where the cacique's writ stops at a line on no official map. You have a *zone* — not a country, not even a county, but ground the state does not freely enter — and holding it turns out to be a different and heavier thing than taking it. A guerrilla that only fights answers to no one. A guerrilla that governs answers to everyone in the valley, every day, in the currency of whether the water works and the harvest is fair and the man who did the killing is punished.

This is the revolution's oldest test, failed by most who reached it: can the people who are good at taking power be trusted with the small, dull, unglamorous holding of it? The first question the valley brings you is the one it has waited generations to ask: *the land — whose is it now?*

- @zona_tierra: The land to those who work it. Redistribute the cacique's holdings through the assembly, in the open — the one act that makes the zone irreversible in the people's hearts.
- @zona_prudente: Hold the land question for after the war. Alienate no one you might still need; administer the zone lightly, and do not create martyrs among the propertied.

@zona_tierra
on-arrival: sup_peasants += 6; pres_guerrero += 3; moral_columnas += 5; disciplina += 3; parque += 2; represion += 3; legitimidad_regimen -= 2; leyenda += 2

The assembly does it itself, which is the whole point — the guerrilla provides the safety and the people provide the justice, the cacique's fences down and the plots walked out by the families who bled on them as peons, the deeds burned in a fire everyone is invited to warm their hands at. It is the deepest thing the war can do: not to promise the land after victory but to *deliver it now*, in the zone, as a working fact, so that every campesino in the valley has a personal, tangible, irreversible reason to keep the soldiers out. The state understands the danger precisely and answers it in force. Let it. You have handed the people something the reprisals cannot take back, because it is already inside them.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@zona_prudente
on-arrival: pres_guerrero += 1; disciplina += 1; sup_peasants += 1; parque += 1

You govern the zone with a light hand and an eye on the propertied you have not yet made enemies of, and it is defensible — a guerrilla does not need to fight the landlord and the army in the same season. It is also the choice that tells the valley the revolution in the sierra is, so far, mostly an armed patience: the soldiers are kept out, but the cacique's map is only suspended, not torn up, and the campesino who risked everything to shelter you notices that his risk has bought him safety but not yet land. You have a zone. You have not yet given the people a reason it is *theirs.*

- @post_event: Continuar.

@justicia_zona
title: La justicia de la zona
