subtitle: The people want a tribunal. What kind of movement holds one?
face-image: img/guardias_blancas.jpg
tags: event
view-if: banda = "" and via = "armada" and armada_entered = 1 and zona_gobernada = 1 and time >= zona_last + 14
priority: 3
frequency: 55
max-visits: 3
on-arrival: zona_last = time

= La justicia de la zona

The zone brings you the case it was always going to bring you: a man the valley has feared for twenty years — a cacique's pistolero, a rapist with a badge, the one who gave the order the last time the army came through — caught, finally, on ground where his protectors cannot reach. The people do not want him handed to a state that would free him by Friday. They want *justice*, and they want it from you, and the word means, in the mouths of people who have never once received it, something with a rope in it.

Here is the revolution's mirror. A movement that refuses is a movement that tells the valley its suffering is still not actionable. A movement that grants it, badly, becomes the thing it fought — a power that kills on the say-so of a crowd. The tribunal you hold, or refuse to hold, is the clearest statement the war will ever make about what it intends to replace the cacique *with*.

- @justicia_tribunal: A real tribunal — public, with a defense, witnesses, a sentence the assembly can live with. Justice as a system, not a settling of scores. Slower, harder, and the only kind worth the name.
- @justicia_pueblo: Give the valley its verdict. The people know what he did; the revolution honors their judgment and does not second-guess a generation of fear.
- @justicia_expulsar: Neither try nor execute — expel him, banish him from the zone under threat. Keep the movement's hands clean, and let the valley wonder if that is mercy or cowardice.

@justicia_tribunal
choose-if: disciplina >= 45
unavailable-subtitle: A real tribunal takes a disciplined movement the assembly respects; without it, any trial you hold is a lynching with minutes.
on-arrival: sup_peasants += 3; legitimidad_regimen -= 2; disciplina += 4; leyenda += 2; political_capital += 2

You hold the hardest kind of court: the accused given a defense, the witnesses heard in order, the crime established rather than assumed, the sentence — real, and heavy, because the crimes are real and heavy — arrived at by a process the valley can see is a process. It is slower than a rope and it is the whole argument of the war made visible: that what the sierra offers is not a better set of masters but a different *kind* of power, one that binds itself to rules even when it does not have to. The valley gets its justice and, more than that, gets its first living glimpse of the thing being fought for. Word of it travels further than any communiqué.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@justicia_pueblo
on-arrival: sup_peasants += 4; represion += 2; disciplina -= 3; paranoia += 3; legitimidad_regimen -= 1; leyenda += 1

You give the valley its verdict, and the valley is not wrong about what he did, and the relief in the assembly is a real and terrible thing to witness — a generation exhaling. It is also the door you did not want opened: a power that kills on the certainty of the crowd, however earned that certainty, has told the crowd that certainty is enough. The next case will be less clear and the crowd no less certain, and the discipline that lets a movement stop short of becoming a mob has been spent, once, on a man who deserved it — which is exactly how it is always first spent. You did justice. You also showed the war a shortcut it will ask to take again.

- @post_event: Continuar.

@justicia_expulsar
on-arrival: disciplina += 1; sup_peasants -= 2; unity += 1

You split the difference and satisfy no one: the man is run out of the zone under threat, alive, which keeps the movement's hands clean and leaves the valley holding the specific bitterness of watching its tormentor walk away on his own feet one more time. It is the choice of a movement that has thought hard about not becoming a killer and not yet hard enough about what it owes the people it governs. He will surface somewhere the state still rules, and he will remember the way out, and the valley will remember that when it finally caught him, the revolution flinched.

- @post_event: Continuar.
